From b914777284b14fad22356763ef9454a28aaa5c18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:55:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] kboot: T6050: hand the internal display over on 27.2

The J714s moves its Linux stub to macOS 27.2 (26B123, mBoot-20457.41.3),
upstream's Mach-O target. The T6050 DCP hand-off admitted 27.0 and 27.3
beta 1 only, so on 27.2 the panel stayed on simpledrm.

Admit 27.2 and publish apple,firmware-compat <27 2 0> (the firmware's own
version), which aurora-silicon/linux iomfb_v27.c keys dcp_methods_27_2 by.
Pin the 27.2 image as 27.0's is pinned: C51FB0C8-C45D-39B0-85BC-520E600FC950,
read from the IPSW. In the J714s identity's Firmware/dcp/t605xdcp.im4p it is
the LC_UUID of the Mach-O at 0x1114608, where 27.0's payload has its pinned
64863924-... at 0x10f8608, and it appears at the same five places in the
payload. dcpext engines must run the same image, as before.

Not booted: no J714s has run a 27.2 stub. If the 27.2 ADT names another
image, the hand-off refuses (simpledrm) and logs the UUID it found.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kboot_display_handoff.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kboot_display_handoff.c b/src/kboot_display_handoff.c
index 1ce1df49..4e7cc77b 100644
--- a/src/kboot_display_handoff.c
+++ b/src/kboot_display_handoff.c
@@ -3240,8 +3240,16 @@ static bool dcp6_dt_describes(void *dt)
  * is taken as the ADT names it, and published with apple,firmware-compat <27 3 0>, the key Linux's
  * firmware-27 DCP driver chooses its 27.3 method table and swap layout by (aurora-silicon/linux
  * #1174). As TripleU613's m1n1 for the J714s does (betizzel's 27.3 handoff).
+ *
+ * 27.2 (26B123, mBoot-20457.41.3) is pinned to its image too, and published with its own
+ * apple,firmware-compat <27 2 0>, the key Linux's 27.2 method table is chosen by. The UUID is the
+ * IPSW's: in the J714s identity's Firmware/dcp/t605xdcp.im4p, the Mach-O that holds 27.0's pinned
+ * UUID (at 0x10f8608, after the 0x10f8000 fileset) sits at 0x1114608 in 26B123, and its UUID
+ * appears at the same five places in the payload as 27.0's does. A J714s whose 27.2 ADT names
+ * another image keeps simpledrm, and Aura's log says which UUID it named.
  */
-#define T6050_DCP_UUID  "64863924-B56B-3E32-87FE-038677F52709"
+#define T6050_DCP_UUID     "64863924-B56B-3E32-87FE-038677F52709"
+#define T6050_DCP_UUID_272 "C51FB0C8-C45D-39B0-85BC-520E600FC950"
 #define T6050_NDISP     5       /* disp0 reg[0..4] are the dcp's disp-0..disp-4 */
 #define T6050_BW_BASE   0x20000 /* bandwidth agent 0's scratch in the PMC metadata */
 #define T6050_BW_STRIDE 0x4000
@@ -3321,12 +3329,16 @@ static T6050_INIT int t6050_check_adt(void)
